    "details": "<p>Some problems don't need another food-delivery app. They need someone who cares enough to build the thing that's missing. HACK FOR GOOD is VYUH 11.0's opening-day open innovation hackathon. Pick any real problem in agriculture, commerce, health or education, build a working prototype, and show us the code and the thinking behind it. The best teams present live on 9 December, in person at IBS Hyderabad or online. Bring a team, an idea and the stubbornness to make it work.</p>\n<p>Domains: 1. Agriculture &middot; 2. Commerce &middot; 3. Health &middot; 4. Education</p>\n<p>Evaluation criteria (both rounds): problem identification &middot; idea &middot; UI/UX &middot; tests &middot; usage of AI and other tech &middot; social impact &middot; feasibility and scalability.</p>\n<p>Prize pool: ₹15,000. Winner ₹10,000 &middot; 1st runner-up ₹5,000.</p>\n<p><strong>Rules and guidelines</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams of 2&ndash;4. Open to UG and PG students from any stream and any college. Cross-college teams are allowed. One team per person.</li>\n<li>Open innovation: any problem within the four domains. Projects may have been started before registration but must be the team's own work. Declare it if the project has been entered in another competition [PROPOSED].</li>\n<li>Round 1 needs all four items: LinkedIn profile links for every member, a public GitHub repository with a README and tests, a working prototype link (deployed app, APK or demo video for hardware), and a pitch deck PDF (max 10 slides + cover, named VYUH11_HACK_TeamName.pdf).</li>\n<li>Broken links, private repositories or prototypes the judges can't open count as missing. No late submissions.</li>\n<li>Libraries, APIs, templates and AI coding assistants are allowed. List them in the README.</li>\n<li>Finalists choose to present in person or online and confirm by 8 Dec, 12:00 PM. Online finalists get a test call on 8 Dec and must keep a backup demo video.</li>\n<li>A finalist team that misses its slot forfeits it.</li>\n<li>Plagiarism, using someone else's project, a faked demo or harassment leads to disqualification.</li>\n<li>Both rounds are judged on: problem identification, idea, UI/UX, tests, usage of AI and other tech, social impact, and feasibility and scalability. Final rankings use the Round 2 score.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The judges' decision is final.</p>",
